%changelog
* Sat Nov 07 2026 Trung Lê <8@tle.id.au> - 153.7.0-1
- Firefox 153.7.0esr, packaged from the Fedora firefox spec to install
  beside the regular Firefox: /usr/bin/firefox-esr, /usr/lib64/firefox-esr,
  its own desktop file, icons and man page; the profile directory is shared
- Add the PPC64LE JIT backend and VSX ports from runlevel5/firefox-ppc64
  153.7.0esr: the JIT with POWER8/POWER9/POWER10 selection at run time,
  Skia and libwebp VSX, the gfx/2d and SWGL AltiVec/VSX kernels, the
  mozglue SIMD string search helpers, encoding_rs SIMD
- Build ppc64le with clang, ThinLTO and PGO for the distribution's default
  CPU baseline; GCC with GNU ld stays available with --without
  build_with_clang
- Drop color-range.patch (it targets a widget file newer than 153) and the
  unused KDE integration patches
